WEBVTT

NOTE Captions for the myVetbuddy film, generated by scripts/make-captions.mjs from the film timeline.

1
00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:03.720
It's seven p.m.

2
00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:08.560
The clinic closed an hour ago,
and there are still eleven notes to write.

3
00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:14.980
At the front desk, WhatsApp doesn't stop.
"Are you open on Saturday?"

4
00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:18.190
"My dog is vomiting." And they all wait.

5
00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:23.380
Reminders live on paper,
or in a spreadsheet.

6
00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:27.840
On a busy week they don't go out,
and pets miss their vaccines.

7
00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:33.260
Appointments sit in a book
or a spreadsheet.

8
00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:36.000
The vet finds out who's next at the door.

9
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:43.260
On a whiteboard, it's four jobs,
all by hand, and none of them talk.

10
00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:44.647
But it's one flow.

11
00:00:44.687 --> 00:00:47.860
A visit becomes a note
and a prescription, then a reminder,

12
00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:50.380
the next appointment,
and WhatsApp in between.

13
00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:53.040
What if all of this happened on its own?

14
00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:00.080
This is VetBuddy.

15
00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:04.160
Press record and examine the pet:
no typing with a dog on the table.

16
00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:06.580
Stop, and the transcript is ready.

17
00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:12.920
It drafts the note
in your clinic's own template,

18
00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:15.240
each section linked
to the words it came from.

19
00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:17.740
Edit anything, then sign off.

20
00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:24.510
Next, the prescription: medicines,

21
00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:28.490
doses and instructions,
as a PDF to print or email.

22
00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:33.720
Set the follow-up, and the owner
gets a WhatsApp reminder.

23
00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:38.410
Have a list already? Upload it.

24
00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:41.130
VetBuddy sorts each
visit into vaccination,

25
00:01:41.170 --> 00:01:43.170
medication, appointment or follow-up,

26
00:01:43.210 --> 00:01:46.890
and attaches the right WhatsApp
template, or drafts a missing one.

27
00:01:46.930 --> 00:01:49.630
Confirm the owners agreed, and schedule.

28
00:01:52.450 --> 00:01:56.010
Every visit lands in Appointments,
a column for each vet.

29
00:01:56.050 --> 00:02:00.703
Book one, and the owner gets a reminder.
Before each visit, the vet gets an alert:

30
00:02:00.743 --> 00:02:04.190
in the app, on WhatsApp,
or in a morning email.

31
00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:13.367
Between visits, the assistant
answers clients on WhatsApp,

32
00:02:13.407 --> 00:02:15.307
from your clinic's profile.

33
00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:19.135
For a health question,
it never gives advice.

34
00:02:19.175 --> 00:02:21.215
It asks what a vet would ask first,

35
00:02:21.255 --> 00:02:24.655
then hands over to your team,
with the answers pinned on top.

36
00:02:24.695 --> 00:02:27.395
Emergencies go straight to a vet.

37
00:02:32.450 --> 00:02:36.017
And when a client is waiting,
VetBuddy drafts replies for your team.

38
00:02:36.057 --> 00:02:38.917
Pick one, change what you like, and send.

39
00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:48.980
Less admin, more time with patients.
Reminders that go out.

40
00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:50.560
Clients answered.

41
00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:55.280
VetBuddy. Less admin, more care.

42
00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:58.580
Find out more at myvetbuddy.com.

